  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n### Request to Add Named HTML Entity: `&rupee;` for U+20B9 (₹)\n\nHello HTML spec maintainers 👋\n\nI'd like to propose the addition of a named character reference `&rupee;` for the Indian Rupee symbol ₹ (Unicode U+20B9) to the HTML Living Standard.\n\n**Why it is important: **\n- Official currency symbol since 2010, supported by Unicode and all modern platforms.\n- India has a large developer base and user population (~1.4B people).\n- Improves developer readability, consistency with other currency entities (`&euro;`, `&yen;`, `&dollar;`, etc.).\n- Reduces need for obscure numeric codes like `&#8377;`.\n\nThanks for considering!\n\nBest,\nHimanshu Kumawat\n",
